  "semantics": {
    "open_world": "Missing relations are UNKNOWN unless a declared, qualified closed-world test proves scoped absence.",
    "negation": "NOT(P) is a candidate statement with its own evidence; lack of evidence for P is never proof of NOT(P).",
    "inversion": "For a directed relation use a typed inverse predicate only when its inverse is defined; SUPPORTS(A,B) does not simply imply SUPPORTS(B,A).",
    "composition": "A→B and B→C can suggest A→C only with a licensed composition rule and evidence class INFERRED/HYPOTHESIS, never automatic OBSERVED.",
    "classification": "Domains overlap; cultural, spiritual and physical categories can be discussed together without collapsing their truth tests.",
    "uncertainty": "An UNKNOWN is an eligible result; unanswerable is not useless.",
    "chaos_drift_evolution": "CHAOS = sensitivity/complex dynamics (hypothesis to test); DRIFT = measurable distribution change over time; EVOLUTION = versioned change with selection/retained lineage. Terms are not interchangeable and each requires an operational definition in empirical use.",
    "metaphysical": "G_d, angelic, mystic and other spiritual classes remain valid interpretive/cultural/hypothesis topics, not sensors or independent being claims.",
    "external_intelligence": "ET candidate signals require terrestrial-source controls, independent replication and scientific review before any extraordinary claim.",
    "token_and_compute": "Logical field size may be vast; budgets, context windows, power, RAM, provider quotas and independent receivers remain finite."
  },
